Description: Web-888 (RX-888) SDR boot chain - FSBL + U-Boot for Debian
 Bootloader package for the Web-888 Debian image (uboot chain): the
 packed boot.bin (source-built Xilinx zynq_fsbl + mainline U-Boot as
 SSBL), the individual FSBL / U-Boot binaries, the compiled boot.scr,
 and the default uEnv.txt, staged under /usr/lib/web888-boot/.
 .
 On configure, the payload is installed onto the FAT boot partition
 mounted at /boot: boot.bin and boot.scr are replaced via
 temp-file + sync + rename with one-generation .bak backups; uEnv.txt
 is only installed when absent (it is the on-device kernel-selection
 knob and user edits are never overwritten). When /boot/boot.bin does
 not exist (chroot / image build) the install step is skipped, so the
 package is safe during rootfs assembly.
 .
 Only the uboot boot chain is supported; the stub chain embeds
 kernel+dtb inside boot.bin and stays rollback-only.

